    {
      "id": "HFB-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Rational reduction gives nonnegative height labels",
      "anchor": "lifts-height-fibres",
      "statement": "For each rational Siegel coset one can choose n integers ℓᵢ with a uniform upper bound m₀ and form the label μᵢ=m₀−ℓᵢ. Its height is at most Cₕ B^(−Σμᵢ), where n is the source rank and B=4^d for d real places of F.",
      "hypotheses": "CM quadratic extension E/F, nondegenerate Hermitian space, doubled form and compact subgroup admitting the specified Iwasawa decomposition. The representatives are rational and distinct modulo the Siegel stabilizer. The dyadic idele is 1/2 at infinity and 1 at finite places.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-height-labelling"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "MSR-04"
      ],
